      "content": "that's a bit a weird way to put it. if the tech progress is \"inevitable\" and \"driven by fundamental science,\" isn't the whole idea of \"steering\" it just a bit of an illusion? it feels like you're saying the outcome is already decided by the tech itself, and humans are just reacting to it. why isn't the policy side treated as a more fundamental driver of how this actually unfolds?",
